    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b2b071a8514c40298ab5fe23838a5ea1",
      "statement": "The frontend manages its WebSocket RPC connection at module scope instead of React state because StrictMode's double effect invocation would create redundant connections; on break, the dead stub is replaced by an RpcPromise wrapping a reconnect loop, and Cap'n Web queues calls pipelined onto the unresolved promise until it resolves.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-frontend/src/main.tsx#L140-L156",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3633c5c64ee15e624d2294dad28a5e905fffcca1c81922d7e08793b7247c8d53:"
        },
