    {
      "id": "claim_a502212b4fc045c9acfcd381fb1596ad",
      "statement": "RPC stubs held in React state must be wrapped in an object because useState's setter invokes any callable value (including a callable RpcStub) to compute state; the repo treats stub disposal via Symbol.dispose (or useEffect cleanup) as mandatory to avoid server-side leaks, and reports unawaited RPC promises (promise pipelining) as intentional rather than floating promises.",
      "evidence": [
